# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FAST-CFD-Computing — what NOT to publish
# These patterns keep build junk and oversized files out of GitHub.
# Nothing here is deleted from your disk — it's just never pushed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Oversized: GitHub hard-rejects any single file > 100 MB ──
# 274 MB scanned book — compress or host externally, then re-add.
**/Pak Studies by M R Kazmi *.pdf

# ── Visual Studio / C++ build output (students dumped whole projects) ──
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Ww]in32/
.vs/
ipch/
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.obj
*.o
*.ilk
*.idb
*.ipch
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlog
*.log
*.suo
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.user
*.vsidx
*.lastbuildstate
*.recipe
*.lock
*.cache
*.res
*.tmp
*.enc

# ── Archives (opaque, bulky — usually project source dumps) ──
# Remove this line if you want to keep specific .zip files, then
# force-add them with:  git add -f "path/to/keep.zip"
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z

# ── OS / editor cruft ──
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*~
